{
    "map": {
        "description": "Generates a JSON string that is stored in the OBSTACLEJSON field on the input Obstruction Identification Surface (OIS) multipatch feature class. This class contains the data necessary to depict obstacles to flight safety within the approach surfaces (in the form of points, lines, or polygons) in the Terrain and Obstacle Profile layout element.",
        "elevation_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The field that will contain base elevation heights of the obstacle features.</p><p>This parameter is used if <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation Source</span> is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation field</span>. The default is the first numeric field in the obstacle feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "elevation_field.title": "Elevation Field",
        "elevation_field_unit.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the linear unit that will be used for the base elevation values. This parameter is used if <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation Source</span> is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation field</span>.</p><ul><li><span title=\"KILOMETERS\">Kilometers</span>—The unit will be kilometers.</li><li><span title=\"METERS\">Meters</span>—The unit will be meters. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"DECIMETERS\">Decimeters</span>—The unit will be decimeters.</li><li><span title=\"CENTIMETERS\">Centimeters</span>—The unit will be centimeters.</li><li><span title=\"MILLIMETERS\">Millimeters</span>—The unit will be millimeters.</li><li><span title=\"NAUTICAL_MILES\">Nautical miles</span>—The unit will be nautical miles.</li><li><span title=\"MILES\">Miles</span>—The unit will be miles.</li><li><span title=\"YARDS\">Yards</span>—The unit will be yards.</li><li><span title=\"FEET\">Feet</span>—The unit will be feet.</li><li><span title=\"INCHES\">Inches</span>—The unit will be inches</li><li><span title=\"DECIMAL_DEGREES\">Decimal degrees</span>—The unit will be decimal degrees.</li><li><span title=\"POINTS\">Points</span>—The unit will be points.</li><li><span title=\"UNKNOWN\">Unknown</span>—The unit will be unknown.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.CENTIMETERS": "Centimeters",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.DECIMAL_DEGREES": "Decimal degrees",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.DECIMETERS": "Decimeters",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.FEET": "Feet",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.INCHES": "Inches",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.KILOMETERS": "Kilometers",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.METERS": "Meters",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.MILES": "Miles",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.MILLIMETERS": "Millimeters",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.NAUTICAL_MILES": "Nautical miles",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.POINTS": "Points",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.UNKNOWN": "Unknown",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.YARDS": "Yards",
        "elevation_field_unit.title": "Elevation Field Units",
        "elevation_option.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how obstacle base elevation heights will be found.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ELEVATION_FIELD\">Elevation field</span>— Base elevation heights will be found in a numeric field of the obstacle feature class.</li><li><span title=\"ELEVATION_DEM\">Elevation DEM</span>— Base elevation heights will be found by deriving them from one or more DEMs. This is the default.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "elevation_option.domain.ELEVATION_DEM": "Elevation DEM",
        "elevation_option.domain.ELEVATION_FIELD": "Elevation field",
        "elevation_option.title": "Elevation Source",
        "height_option.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how obstacle height values will be measured.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ABSOLUTE_HEIGHT\">Absolute height</span>— Obstacle heights will be measured from sea level.</li><li><span title=\"RELATIVE_HEIGHT\">Relative height</span>— Obstacle heights will be measured from ground level. This is the default.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "height_option.domain.ABSOLUTE_HEIGHT": "Absolute height",
        "height_option.domain.RELATIVE_HEIGHT": "Relative height",
        "height_option.title": "Obstacle Feature Height Type",
        "in_dems.descr": "<xdoc><p>The DEMs covering the obstacles that will be used to derive base elevation values. This parameter is used if <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation Source</span> is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation DEM</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_dems.title": "Input Elevation Model",
        "in_flightpath_features.descr": "The polyline features that will define curved approaches to the specified runways. If no features are provided, all input features will be processed as straight approaches.",
        "in_flightpath_features.title": "Input Flight Path Features",
        "in_obstacle_features.descr": "The input obstacle features that will be analyzed. The feature class must be z-enabled.",
        "in_obstacle_features.title": "Input Obstacle Features",
        "in_runway_features.descr": "The input runway dataset. The feature class must be z-enabled and contain polylines.",
        "in_runway_features.title": "Input Runway Features",
        "label_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>A field from the input obstacle feature class that will be used to label the obstacle. When an obstacle JSON generated by this tool is later used to create a Terrain and Obstacle Profile element in a layout, the data from the field provided will be used to label the input point obstacles in that element.</p><p>This parameter only applies when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Obstacle Features</span> parameter values contain point features. <note type=\"note\"/><p group=\"note\">If no field is provided, the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">ObjectID</span> field will be applied by default.</p></p></xdoc>",
        "label_field.title": "Obstacle Labels",
        "obstacle_height_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the field that will contain the height of the obstacle features or the keyword FEATURE_GEOMETRY to indicate obstacle feature geometry z-coordinate values.</p><ul><li><span title=\"FEATURE_GEOMETRY\">Feature Geometry</span>—The field that will contain the height of the obstacle features.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "obstacle_height_field.domain.FEATURE_GEOMETRY": "Feature Geometry",
        "obstacle_height_field.title": "Obstacle Height",
        "obstacle_height_unit.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the obstacle height unit of measure that will be used.</p><ul><li><span title=\"KILOMETERS\">Kilometers</span>—The unit will be kilometers.</li><li><span title=\"METERS\">Meters</span>—The unit will be meters.</li><li><span title=\"DECIMETERS\">Decimeters</span>—The unit will be decimeters.</li><li><span title=\"CENTIMETERS\">Centimeters</span>—The unit will be centimeters.</li><li><span title=\"MILLIMETERS\">Millimeters</span>—The unit will be millimeters.</li><li><span title=\"NAUTICAL_MILES\">Nautical Miles</span>—The unit will be nautical miles.</li><li><span title=\"MILES\">Miles</span>—The unit will be miles.</li><li><span title=\"YARDS\">Yards</span>—The unit will be yards.</li><li><span title=\"FEET\">Feet</span>—The unit will be feet.</li><li><span title=\"INCHES\">Inches</span>—The unit will be inches</li><li><span title=\"DECIMAL_DEGREES\">Decimal Degrees</span>—The unit will be decimal degrees.</li><li><span title=\"POINTS\">Points</span>—The unit will be points.</li><li><span title=\"UNKNOWN\">Unknown</span>—The unit will be unknown.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.CENTIMETERS": "Centimeters",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.DECIMAL_DEGREES": "Decimal Degrees",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.DECIMETERS": "Decimeters",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.FEET": "Feet",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.INCHES": "Inches",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.KILOMETERS": "Kilometers",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.METERS": "Meters",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.MILES": "Miles",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.MILLIMETERS": "Millimeters",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.NAUTICAL_MILES": "Nautical Miles",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.POINTS": "Points",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.UNKNOWN": "Unknown",
        "obstacle_height_unit.domain.YARDS": "Yards",
        "obstacle_height_unit.title": "Unit",
        "obstacle_output_method.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the obstacles that will be included in the output feature class.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ALL_OBSTACLES\">All obstacles</span>—All obstacles within the extent of the OIS will be included in the output.</li><li><span title=\"PENETRATING_OBSTACLES\">Penetrating obstacles</span>—Only obstacles that penetrate the OIS will be included in the output.</li><li><span title=\"SHADOWING_OBSTACLES\">Shadowing obstacles</span>—Only obstacles that shadow other obstacles will be included in the output.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "obstacle_output_method.domain.ALL_OBSTACLES": "All obstacles",
        "obstacle_output_method.domain.PENETRATING_OBSTACLES": "Penetrating obstacles",
        "obstacle_output_method.domain.SHADOWING_OBSTACLES": "Shadowing obstacles",
        "obstacle_output_method.title": "Obstacle Output Method",
        "out_ois_features.title": "Output OIS Features",
        "params.category1": "Shadow Calculation Parameters",
        "shadow_horizontal_distance.descr": "The length of the approach surface in meters (calculated from the runway end) where shadows are considered horizontally aligned.",
        "shadow_horizontal_distance.title": "Horizontal Distance",
        "shadow_slope.descr": "<xdoc><p>The slope of the shadow that will be considered past the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Horizontal Distance</span> parameter value.</p></xdoc>",
        "shadow_slope.title": "Slope",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Generates a JSON string that is stored in the <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">OBSTACLEJSON</span> field on the input Obstruction Identification Surface (OIS) multipatch feature class. This class contains the data necessary to depict obstacles to flight safety within the approach surfaces (in the form of points, lines, or polygons) in the Terrain and Obstacle Profile layout element.</p><p>For each runway feature, the tool identifies each approach surface associated with that runway. For each approach surface, the tool uses the underlying elevation models and input obstacle features to determine the highest elevations and heights of those obstacle features that intersect the approach surfaces extent. The resulting 3D geometry, representing the highest-point cross section of each affected obstacle, are created and stored in JSON format and saved in the corresponding approach OIS feature.</p><p>The use of Obstacle Point feature input may be preferred since it populates additional <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">OBSTACLEJSON</span> fields and allows for labeling of obstacles within a Terrain and Profile Element.</p></xdoc>",
        "target_ois_features.descr": "The multipatch features with defined airport data model schema. The feature class must be z-enabled.",
        "target_ois_features.title": "Target OIS Features",
        "title": "Generate OIS Obstacle Data"
    }
}
